  "Question": "If \\(3(4x+5\\pi)=P,\\) then \\(6(8x+10\\pi)=\\)",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(2P\\)",
    "B": "\\(4P\\)",
    "C": "\\(6P\\)",
    "D": "\\(8P\\)",
    "E": "\\(18P\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "B",
  "Solution": "The distributive property gives \\(8x+10\\pi=2(4x+5\\pi)\\). This lets us keep the given expression together:\n\\[\n6(8x+10\\pi)\n=6\\cdot2(4x+5\\pi)\n=4[3(4x+5\\pi)]\n=4P.\n\\]\nThus the answer is \\(\\boxed{4P}\\), choice B.",
